the impact of the outbreak can also be  felt on Capitol Hill Georgia congressman  Doug Holland is one of several  Republicans who have decided self  quarantine after coming into contact  with an affected person at CPAC joining  us now live from his home is our  headliner this morning ranking member of  the House Judiciary Committee and Senate  candidate Doug Collins appreciate your  time this morning  appreciate you skyping in considering  you are staying in why did you decide to  do that we did so out of a bunch cause  it's good to see you though and because  we came in contact it's been two weeks  ago today in fact today is my last day  I'll be back out tomorrow I'm  asymptomatic I don't have any I've never  had any symptoms of the virus but what  we wanted to do was make sure it four  out of abundance of caution stay in and  emphasize to everyone if they follow the  rules they follow the protocols that are  set out that we can manage this virus  and we can do what is right and I think  by doing this we're setting the example  to say others don't take it lightly take  it seriously but also don't panic make  sure you're doing the right things  washing your hands staying away if  you're sick and if you are sick go to  the doctor and get tested yeah a very  important advice and we're certainly  concerned about your health and the  health of all lawmakers staff everyone  around the country obviously but this is  also happening in a context where in the  last moment we've just gotten a new  statement from senator Ted Cruz he's  also been self quarantined as you know I  believe in Texas he's now saying that  his DC office is going to close  temporarily senator Romney has done the  same there's at least one case of  somebody who's tested positive for  coronavirus in the office of democratic  senator maria cantwell so it's happening  in that context as congressman while  Wall Street is also suffering a very  volatile day right now and a lot of  people around the country are looking to  you and other lawmakers to get the  nation's business done and in working on  an economic proposal that the president  wants how do you balance all that sir  well it's been a large balance and I  think I've been at work all week down  here we've had other bills on the floor  this week FISA bills and also now  working I was just on conference call of  my colleagues concerning our response  look I think you'll see a lot of other  offices especially next week we're not  supposed to be in next week you'll see  probably a lot of staffs working from  home probably and we're discussing that  right now  my office and make sure there are DC  office because your Wilson we're already  starting to see it a couple of cases it  looks like now on spouse on the Senate  side that and others so is it is a very  real concern we want to stop it in its  tracks this is why the protocols are in  place so we can identify those that are  sick isolate them get them better and so  that others aren't infected but in  dealing with also this economic side the  president made it very clear last night  that he is willing to help but he wants  to help in the proper ways simply  throwing money in this situation right  now without having a proper oversight  even Democrats last night in the Rules  Committee we're very concerned about the  fact that no hearings or anything were  involved in this we won't work  bipartisan together to make sure the  American people have what they need from  an economic standpoint but we also it  needs to be targeted to make sure that  the economic stimulus of economic  progress here is not simply just  throwing money in a problem without any  real solutions to making the economy or  helping those who need help well you can  assume the markets looking for a  solution because as you've been speaking  the Dow has been off more than 2000  points and we can now report that the  Dow has fallen to its lowest level since  July 2017 so looking at multi-year lows  here and I'll let you know that our  reporting from Capitol Hill as of this  moment is that GOP leaders McCarthy and  McConnell oppose House Democrats  coronavirus bill the status of the bill  is now in limbo congressman how do you  respond in this as well and mr.  McConnell again we need a stimulus  package but we also need something that  actually will work there's nothing that  we've seen so far that actually stems  this time simply putting money into  unemployment insurance when you have  unemployment unemployment claims that  their lowest these are things that you  work on as the situation develops we  needed a stimulus now that if it works  help small businesses make sure that you  get extended leave those are the kind of  things that could work into this bill  but right now we've not been able to  partner on this like we did with the  steam of the coronavirus package from  last week in which we provided funds for  the actual attacking of the virus and  the response to that virus that was  bipartisan over 400 votes there's no  reason why we can't do this today and  work on that as we go forward and I know  McCarthy and others has talked to us and  Kevin Brady and others talked to us on  the conference call about why this is  not a package that at this point we can  support but I know the president is  committed to finding something that is  possibly going to work in our leadership  is committed to working with a Democrat  leadership to find that markets will be  aware of that and I think we just need  to make sure that we have a focused  response and only that's what the  administration is giving Congress  congressman in fact you just mentioned  the the House Republican leader Kevin  McCarthy we expect him to hold a news  conference live in the next few moments  we of course will go there live to hear  what he's saying about these economic  plans about the health response as well  of course Speaker Nancy Pelosi expected  to have a news conference later in the  hour we'll go there as well to hear from  both sides you're laying out the  important economic response and what you  want to see happen what about the health  response about a week ago you were with  the president in your home state there  in Georgia at the CDC headquarters and  we've been hearing from the  administration that they're prepared on  testing and then if you want to be  tested you can be tested for the corona  virus but a few moments ago Sandra  interviewed it interviewed Republican  senator John Barrasso who as you know is  not just the senator he's a doctor and  he said he still has concerns that the  CDC can really follow through on that  what assurances can you give the  American people this morning well they  sure said I have straight from the CDC  and working with the listing to the non  the president the vice president the  task force and watching this closely the  cdc's of course in my home state we  never forget this is the group that also  just a few years ago was able to get  under control the Ebola virus and others  these are not people who are honored to  customed to dealing with hard issues and  they're dealing with it and I think the  issue that we have now is is we need to  make sure testing is there for those  that are sick well we don't need to have  is rushing our health care system and  rushing the public health system with  folks who are just wondering if they  have the virus if you're sick you have  condition flu-like vision symptoms and  go get tested but I think right now if  the testing is it's ramping up the more  test kits are available we'll be able to  make sure that anyone who has those  symptoms are being able to be tested  I trust the CDC it's always as we look  forward to we make sure that it is  happening in real time  they're putting for the results I think  we'll see over time as that works out  but right now I  every confidence that the public health  officials all across this country in  every state are doing everything they  possibly can to make sure that they  identify the proper cases make sure  they're properly quarantined make sure  they're promptly being treated  therapeutics are being developed and a  long term me vaccine is being looked at  as well the big thing for people is is  to not panic in this but also to make  sure that they're doing what is  responsible and one of the biggest  things I've told people this for the  whole week that I've been here is some  of the simplest things are things that  sometimes you forget when you believe  it's some big crisis this goes back to  simple basic personal hygiene go back to  the sink you wash your hands don't go  out and call for people if you're sick  stay away and if you're if you are sick  make sure that you're treated those are  the ways that we can make sure that we  isolate this stop it it will continue to  grow but we can do so in at a much  slower pace than we've seen in the rest  of it a lot more about the spread of it  and how long can live in the air things  we didn't even know yesterday or a week  ago so congressman there's still a lot  to take in as you can see markets taking  all of this in this morning we wish you  well as you finish off your self  quarantine there and and Ted Cruz I  think finishes his this afternoon while  he's also shutting down his office now  we appreciate it congressman thank you  for coming on sir

